    "answer": {
      "short": "Rob: 16 years; Ed: 20 years.",
      "worked": "Their age difference stays the same. It represents one part in both $4:5$ and $5:6$, so the value of one part is unchanged. Each age increases by one part in 4 years.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}1\\text{ part}&=4\\text{ years}\\\\\\text{Rob's age}&=4\\times4=16\\text{ years}\\\\\\text{Ed's age}&=5\\times4=20\\text{ years}\\end{align*}$$\n\nCheck: in 4 years, their ages are 20 and 24, and $20:24=5:6$.",
